IMPORT prelude

-- COVID-19 (Temporary Measures) Act 2020 (Singapore) -- the temporary relief a person or business met: which contracts were covered
-- (s 4, First Schedule para 1), the moratorium on a counterparty's actions after a notification for relief (ss 5(1) to (3), 5(7), 9(1)),
-- performance bonds and liquidated damages under construction and supply contracts (s 6(2), (3), (5)), deposits and cancellation fees
-- under event and tourism contracts (s 7(2) to (4)), what happens to an action taken in breach (s 8(2) to (6)), lawyers before an
-- assessor (s 14), which leases got Part 2A rental relief and how relief for rent already paid is applied (ss 19C, 19H(2)), the
-- offences and their maxima (ss 8(1), 19W, 34(7), 35(9) to (11), 106), and when Parts 2 and 7 ran out (s 1(2A), (7)).
--
-- Edition: informal consolidation, "version in force from 1/7/2026", as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/COVID19TMA2020.txt (retrieved 1 October 2026; the deposit's metadata calls it the current version as at
-- 1 October 2026). The Act is still printed as "No. 14 of 2020", not as a Revised Edition. The latest amendment annotated is Act 15 of
-- 2026 wef 1 July 2026 (s 2 "Minister", and the repeal of Parts 8C and 10A).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0120 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is long (about 170 pages, Parts 1 to 12 with five Schedules) and almost wholly temporary: SCOPED to Part 2
-- (relief for inability to perform contracts), the entry and relief rules of Part 2A (rental relief), the offences, and the Part 7
-- control-order penalties that every resident lived under in 2020 to 2022.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: ss 1A to 1C (late applications); s 3 beyond its effect (the prescribed period itself is fixed by Gazette order and is
-- an input here); s 5(4) to (6), (8) to (14) (regulation-made carve-outs, stay of pending proceedings, insolvency look-back
-- extensions, para 1(a)/(b) loan limitation); s 5A (inability to exercise a right -- applies only to prescribed contracts); s 6(4), (6),
-- (7); s 7A(2) to (4) and 7B (interest caps and holding-over amounts are left to regulations); the assessor machinery in ss 10 to 13A,
-- 15A to 19; Part 2A beyond ss 19C, 19H(2) and 19W (cash grants, additional relief, reversal, statutory repayment schedules, security
-- deposits); Part 3 (insolvency thresholds, expired after one year); Parts 4 and 5 (remote meetings and hearings); Part 6 (property tax
-- remission pass-through); s 34(1) to (6) and s 35(1) to (8) beyond their effect (what a control order may say, enforcement powers);
-- Parts 8, 8A, 8B (construction delay, extension of time, cost-sharing); Part 9 (collective sales); Part 10 (renegotiation of specified
-- contracts); Part 12 (2021 rental waiver) beyond s 106; the Schedules other than para 1 of the First. No regulation or Gazette order
-- was retrieved, so every "prescribed" period, rate or amount is an input.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill conventions (by way of the example rows). No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `COVID-19 (Temporary Measures) Act 2020 -- relief`

GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the positive part` MEANS
    IF `amount` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `amount` ELSE 0

GIVEN `first` IS A NUMBER, `second` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS
    IF `first` AT MOST `second` THEN `first` ELSE `second`

§§ `s 1(2A), (7) -- when the temporary Parts ran out`

-- s 1(2A): "Parts 1 (except section 2) and 2 remain in force until the end of 19 April 2022." s 1(7): "Part 7 remains in force until
-- the end of 8 April 2024." (s 1(3): expiry does not affect things previously done, and ss 7B, 8 and others survive it.) Dates are
-- written as numbers YYYYMMDD.
GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 2 relief is still in force on` IF
    `the date` AT MOST 20220419

GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 7 control orders are still in force on` IF
    `the date` AT MOST 20240408

§§ `s 2, s 4 and First Schedule para 1 -- scheduled contracts`

-- First Schedule para 1: scheduled contracts are (a) a bank or finance company loan facility "to an enterprise" secured on
-- "commercial or industrial immovable property located in Singapore"; (b) the same secured on plant, machinery or fixed assets used
-- for manufacturing, production or other business purposes; (c) a performance bond under a construction or supply contract; (d) a
-- hire-purchase or conditional sales agreement of such plant, machinery or fixed asset, or of a commercial vehicle; (da) a lease of
-- such plant, machinery or fixed asset, or of a commercial vehicle "except (A) a private hire car ... and (B) a taxi"; (e) an event
-- contract; (f) a tourism-related contract; (g) a construction contract or supply contract; (h) "a lease or licence of
-- non-residential immovable property"; (i), (j) a housing developer's option, or sale and purchase agreement, for housing units;
-- (k), (l) the same from a commercial developer for commercial units.
-- s 2: "event contract" covers venue, accommodation, catering and the like for a business meeting, conference, "concert, show,
-- wedding, party or other social gathering, or sporting event"; "tourism-related contract" covers international carriage of
-- passengers by sea or land, and transport, short-term accommodation, dining, tours etc. for visitors and tourists.
-- A home loan, a residential tenancy, a personal loan or an ordinary consumer purchase is in none of these descriptions.
DECLARE Contract IS ONE OF
    `a bank loan to an enterprise secured on a factory or office`
    `a bank loan to an enterprise secured on business machinery`
    `a performance bond under a construction contract`
    `a hire-purchase of a commercial vehicle`
    `a lease of business machinery`
    `a lease of a private hire car`
    `a lease of a taxi`
    `a wedding banquet booking`
    `a tour package for outbound tourists`
    `a construction contract`
    `a lease of a shop`
    `a housing developer's option to purchase a flat`
    `a commercial developer's sale of an office unit`
    `a home loan secured on a flat`
    `a lease of a residential flat`
    `a personal loan`
    `a mobile phone subscription`

GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract is a scheduled contract` IF
    CONSIDER `the contract`
    WHEN `a lease of a private hire car` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a lease of a taxi` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a home loan secured on a flat` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a lease of a residential flat` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a personal loan` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a mobile phone subscription` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract is a lease of non-residential property` IF
    CONSIDER `the contract`
    WHEN `a lease of a shop` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 4(1): "This Part does not apply to -- (a) a lease or licence of non-residential immovable property entered into or renewed (other
-- than automatically or in exercise of a right of renewal in the lease or licence) on or after 25 March 2020; or (b) any other
-- scheduled contract entered into or renewed (other than automatically) on or after 25 March 2020."
-- So a right of renewal saves a shop lease but not any other scheduled contract.
DECLARE Making IS ONE OF
    `made or renewed by fresh agreement`
    `renewed automatically`
    `renewed in exercise of a right of renewal`

GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract, `made or renewed on` IS A NUMBER, `how` IS A Making
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 2 applies to the contract` IF
        `the contract is a scheduled contract` `the contract`
    AND (   `made or renewed on` LESS THAN 20200325
         OR CONSIDER `how`
            WHEN `renewed automatically` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `renewed in exercise of a right of renewal` THEN `the contract is a lease of non-residential property` `the contract`
            OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `ss 5(1), 9(1) -- when the moratorium applies`

-- s 5(1): the section applies where "(a) a party to a scheduled contract (called in this Division A) is or will be unable to perform
-- an obligation in the contract ... being an obligation that is to be performed on or after 1 February 2020; (b) the inability is to a
-- material extent caused by a COVID-19 event; and (c) A has served a notification for relief in accordance with section 9(1) on --
-- (i) the other party or parties to the contract; (ii) any guarantor or surety for A's obligation in the contract; and (iii) such other
-- person as may be prescribed." (1A): for an event or tourism contract, A's inability to hold the event or accept the goods or
-- services on the agreed date counts as an inability to perform. s 9(1): the notification must be served "within the period specified
-- in regulations", "whether with or without prior demand for performance".
GIVEN `Part 2 applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `obligation due on` IS A NUMBER, `materially caused by a COVID-19 event` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `notification served on the other party` IS A BOOLEAN, `notification served on any guarantor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5 relief applies` IF
        `Part 2 applies`
    AND `obligation due on` AT LEAST 20200201
    AND `materially caused by a COVID-19 event`
    AND `notification served on the other party`
    AND `notification served on any guarantor`

§§ `s 5(2), (3) -- the actions the other party may not take`

-- s 5(2): "Despite any law or anything in the contract, another party to the contract (called in this Division B) may not take any
-- action described in subsection (3) in relation to the subject inability until after the earliest of the following: (a) the expiry
-- of the prescribed period; (b) the withdrawal by A of A's notification for relief; (c) on an application under section 9(2), the
-- assessor makes a determination that the case in question is not one to which this section applies."
-- s 5(3): (a) court action against A or A's guarantor or surety; (b) arbitration; (c) enforcing security over immovable property;
-- (d) enforcing security over movable property "used for the purpose of a trade, business or profession"; (e) to (h) a creditors'
-- scheme meeting, judicial management, winding up or bankruptcy application; (i) appointing a receiver or manager; (j) execution,
-- distress or other legal process "except with the leave of the court"; (k) repossessing goods under chattels leasing, hire-purchase or
-- retention of title "being goods used for the purpose of a trade, business or profession" (example: a private hire car on
-- hire-purchase); (l) terminating a lease or licence of immovable property for non-payment of rent; (m) re-entry or forfeiture; (n)
-- enforcing a judgment, arbitral award or adjudication determination; (o) anything prescribed.
-- Not in the list: a letter of demand, and (outside s 7A(5)) terminating any contract other than a lease for non-payment.
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    `suing A in court`
    `starting an arbitration against A`
    `enforcing a mortgage over A's factory`
    `enforcing a charge over A's business machinery`
    `applying to wind up A`
    `making a bankruptcy application against A's guarantor`
    `appointing a receiver over A's business`
    `levying execution on A's property without leave of court`
    `repossessing A's private hire car under hire-purchase`
    `terminating A's shop lease for unpaid rent`
    `re-entering A's shop`
    `enforcing a judgment against A`
    `sending A a letter of demand`
    `repossessing goods A uses only at home`

GIVEN `the action` IS A Action
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action is one section 5 holds back` IF
    CONSIDER `the action`
    WHEN `sending A a letter of demand` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `repossessing goods A uses only at home` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Day numbers (any consecutive count of days) are used for the timing rules below. A withdrawal or determination that has not happened
-- is passed as FALSE with any day.
GIVEN `prescribed period ends on day` IS A NUMBER,
      `notification withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN, `withdrawn on day` IS A NUMBER,
      `assessor found section 5 does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN, `found on day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day the moratorium ends` MEANS
    IF `notification withdrawn` AND `assessor found section 5 does not apply`
    THEN `the smaller of` (`the smaller of` `prescribed period ends on day` `withdrawn on day`) `found on day`
    ELSE IF `notification withdrawn`
         THEN `the smaller of` `prescribed period ends on day` `withdrawn on day`
         ELSE IF `assessor found section 5 does not apply`
              THEN `the smaller of` `prescribed period ends on day` `found on day`
              ELSE `prescribed period ends on day`

-- "until after the earliest of": an action on the very day the moratorium ends is read as still barred (a reading, not a holding).
GIVEN `relief applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `the action` IS A Action, `taken on day` IS A NUMBER, `moratorium ends on day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the other party is barred from the action` IF
        `relief applies`
    AND `the action is one section 5 holds back` `the action`
    AND `taken on day` AT MOST `moratorium ends on day`

-- s 5(7): "Any period of limitation prescribed by any law or in any contract for the taking of an action in relation to the subject
-- inability is extended by a period equal to the period beginning on the date of service by A of the notification for relief ... and
-- ending on the earliest of" the same three events. Counted here as end day minus service day.
GIVEN `served on day` IS A NUMBER, `moratorium ends on day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the extension of the limitation period in days` MEANS
    `the positive part` (`moratorium ends on day` MINUS `served on day`)

§§ `s 6(2), (3), (5) -- construction and supply contracts`

-- s 6(2): B "may not make a call on the performance bond or equivalent in relation to the subject inability at any time earlier than 7
-- days before" its expiry date (as stated, or as extended). (3): if A applies to the issuer "not less than 7 days before the date of
-- expiry ... to extend the term" and serves notice of the application on B at the same time, "the term ... is extended to a date that is
-- 7 days after the end of the prescribed period, or such other date as may be agreed between A, B and the issuer". (4): (2) stops
-- applying once the notification is withdrawn or an assessor finds s 5 inapplicable.
GIVEN `relief applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `call on day` IS A NUMBER, `bond expires on day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the call on the performance bond is premature` IF
        `relief applies`
    AND `call on day` LESS THAN `bond expires on day` MINUS 7

-- The text says "extended to" the new date; where that date would fall before the stated expiry the text does not say what happens,
-- and no such case is tested.
GIVEN `bond expires on day` IS A NUMBER, `applied to issuer on day` IS A NUMBER, `notice served on B at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `prescribed period ends on day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the expiry day of the performance bond` MEANS
    IF `applied to issuer on day` AT MOST `bond expires on day` MINUS 7 AND `notice served on B at the same time`
    THEN `prescribed period ends on day` PLUS 7
    ELSE `bond expires on day`

-- s 6(5): "for the purposes of calculating the liquidated damages payable under the contract or assessing other damages in respect of
-- the subject inability, where the subject inability occurs on or after 1 February 2020 but before the expiry of the prescribed period,
-- any period for which the subject inability subsists and falling within that period is to be disregarded in determining the period
-- of delay in performance by A." Days of inability inside the window are an input.
GIVEN `days of delay` IS A NUMBER, `days of inability within the window` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the delay counted for damages in days` MEANS
    `the positive part` (`days of delay` MINUS `days of inability within the window`)

GIVEN `days of delay` IS A NUMBER, `days of inability within the window` IS A NUMBER, `liquidated damages per day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the liquidated damages payable` MEANS
    `the delay counted for damages in days` `days of delay` `days of inability within the window` TIMES `liquidated damages per day`

§§ `s 7(2) to (4) -- event and tourism contracts`

-- s 7(2): the other party "may not, after being served with the notification for relief ..., at any time (whether during or after the
-- prescribed period) forfeit any deposit ... on the basis of the subject inability, unless the notification for relief is withdrawn or
-- an assessor has made a determination that the forfeiture of the deposit or any part of the deposit is just and equitable". (3): a
-- deposit already forfeited, "including at any time between 1 February 2020 and the date of commencement of this Part", must "as soon
-- as practicable" be restored. (4): COVID-19 causation "is a defence to a claim for the payment of a cancellation fee"; (4A): not if the
-- notification is withdrawn or an assessor finds s 5 inapplicable or the fee just and equitable.
GIVEN `notification served` IS A BOOLEAN, `notification withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN, `assessor found forfeiture just and equitable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deposit may be kept` IF
        (NOT `notification served`)
    OR  `notification withdrawn`
    OR  `assessor found forfeiture just and equitable`

GIVEN `materially caused by a COVID-19 event` IS A BOOLEAN, `notification withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `assessor found section 5 does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN, `assessor found the fee just and equitable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a defence to the cancellation fee` IF
        `materially caused by a COVID-19 event`
    AND (NOT `notification withdrawn`)
    AND (NOT `assessor found section 5 does not apply`)
    AND (NOT `assessor found the fee just and equitable`)

§§ `s 8(2) to (6) -- what becomes of an action taken in breach`

-- s 8(2): proceedings commenced in breach of s 5(2) "must, on the lodgment of a copy of the notification for relief ..., be
-- dismissed". (3): enforcement of security in breach "is void except as against a bona fide purchaser for value without notice of the
-- notification for relief". (4): void -- appointment of a receiver or manager, forfeiture in breach of s 5A(2), a call on a performance
-- bond in breach of s 6(2), forfeiture of a deposit in breach of s 7(2). (5): invalid -- repossession of goods, termination for
-- non-payment of rent or other moneys, re-entry or forfeiture. (6): termination in breach of s 7A(5) is invalid.
DECLARE Breach IS ONE OF
    `court proceedings begun during the moratorium`
    `a sale of mortgaged property to a buyer with notice`
    `a sale of mortgaged property to a bona fide purchaser without notice`
    `a receiver appointed during the moratorium`
    `a premature call on a performance bond`
    `a forfeited event deposit`
    `a repossession during the moratorium`
    `a lease terminated for unpaid rent during the moratorium`

DECLARE Consequence IS ONE OF
    `dismissed on lodging the notification`
    `void`
    `invalid`
    `stands`

GIVEN `the breach` IS A Breach
GIVETH A Consequence
`the consequence of the breach` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the breach`
    WHEN `court proceedings begun during the moratorium` THEN `dismissed on lodging the notification`
    WHEN `a sale of mortgaged property to a buyer with notice` THEN `void`
    WHEN `a sale of mortgaged property to a bona fide purchaser without notice` THEN `stands`
    WHEN `a receiver appointed during the moratorium` THEN `void`
    WHEN `a premature call on a performance bond` THEN `void`
    WHEN `a forfeited event deposit` THEN `void`
    WHEN `a repossession during the moratorium` THEN `invalid`
    WHEN `a lease terminated for unpaid rent during the moratorium` THEN `invalid`

§§ `s 14 -- lawyers before an assessor`

-- s 14: "No party may be represented by an advocate and solicitor at proceedings before an assessor, except with the permission of the
-- assessor." (s 15: each party bears its own costs.)
GIVEN `the assessor permits it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a party may be represented by a lawyer before the assessor` IF
    `the assessor permits it`

§§ `s 19C -- leases that get Part 2A rental relief`

-- s 19C(1): Part 2A "applies to a lease agreement for a prescribed property that is in force during the relevant period (or any part of
-- it) and -- (a) is entered into, or renewed, before 25 March 2020; or (b) is entered into before 25 March 2020, and is renewed on or
-- after 25 March 2020, either automatically or in exercise of a right of renewal in the lease agreement." s 19B: the "relevant period"
-- starts on 1 April 2020 and ends on a prescribed date; whether the property is "prescribed" is an input.
DECLARE Renewal IS ONE OF
    `not renewed`
    `renewed by fresh agreement`
    `renewed automatically or under a right of renewal`

GIVEN `prescribed property` IS A BOOLEAN, `in force during the relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN, `entered into on` IS A NUMBER,
      `renewal` IS A Renewal, `renewed on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 2A applies to the lease` IF
        `prescribed property`
    AND `in force during the relevant period`
    AND `entered into on` LESS THAN 20200325
    AND CONSIDER `renewal`
        WHEN `not renewed` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `renewed automatically or under a right of renewal` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `renewed by fresh agreement` THEN `renewed on` LESS THAN 20200325

§§ `s 19H(2) -- rental relief`

-- s 19H(2): "(a) the tenant is not liable for rent that is payable under the lease agreement for the prescribed period of an amount up to
-- the prescribed amount ...; (b) if the tenant has already paid ... any rent for all or any part of the prescribed period ..., then the
-- rent payable by the tenant for the remaining period of the lease agreement is reduced by the amount paid up to the prescribed amount
-- (called in this section the deductible amount) ...; (c) ... the rent payable for the earliest period of time ... is reduced first ...;
-- and (d) if paragraph (b) is inapplicable, or there is any balance of the deductible amount remaining after any reduction under that
-- paragraph, the tenant's landlord must immediately refund to the tenant the deductible amount or the balance". (3): the relief is "not
-- limited to or determined by the amount of cash grant". The prescribed amount is an input.
GIVEN `rent for the prescribed period` IS A NUMBER, `prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rent waived` MEANS
    `the smaller of` `rent for the prescribed period` `prescribed amount`

GIVEN `rent already paid for the prescribed period` IS A NUMBER, `prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deductible amount` MEANS
    `the smaller of` `rent already paid for the prescribed period` `prescribed amount`

GIVEN `rent already paid for the prescribed period` IS A NUMBER, `prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER, `rent for the remaining period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reduction of future rent` MEANS
    `the smaller of` (`the deductible amount` `rent already paid for the prescribed period` `prescribed amount`) `rent for the remaining period`

GIVEN `rent already paid for the prescribed period` IS A NUMBER, `prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER, `rent for the remaining period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the refund the landlord owes` MEANS
    `the deductible amount` `rent already paid for the prescribed period` `prescribed amount`
    MINUS `the reduction of future rent` `rent already paid for the prescribed period` `prescribed amount` `rent for the remaining period`

§§ `ss 8(1), 19W, 34(7), 35(9) to (11), 106 -- offences`

-- s 8(1): contravening s 5(2), 5A(2), 6(2), 7(2) or (3) or 7A(5) "without reasonable excuse" -- "a fine not exceeding $1,000" (no
-- imprisonment). s 19W(1) (Part 2A) and s 106(1) (Part 12): a declaration, statement, information or document "false or misleading in a
-- material particular", knowing, ought reasonably to know, or reckless -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term
-- not exceeding 12 months or ... both". s 34(7): contravening a control order without reasonable excuse -- "(a) a fine not exceeding
-- $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or ... both; or (b) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, ... a
-- fine not exceeding $20,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or ... both". s 35(9), (10), (11): an individual,
-- or a body corporate, association or partnership, failing without reasonable excuse to comply with an enforcement officer's direction
-- -- the same maxima. Only s 34(7) and s 35(11) step up for a repeat offence.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `suing or enforcing during the moratorium`
    `calling a performance bond early`
    `forfeiting or not restoring an event deposit`
    `a false declaration for rental relief`
    `a false declaration for rental waiver`
    `breaching a control order`
    `an individual disobeying an enforcement officer`
    `a business disobeying an enforcement officer`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `second or subsequent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `suing or enforcing during the moratorium` THEN 1000
    WHEN `calling a performance bond early` THEN 1000
    WHEN `forfeiting or not restoring an event deposit` THEN 1000
    WHEN `a false declaration for rental relief` THEN 5000
    WHEN `a false declaration for rental waiver` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE IF `second or subsequent` THEN 20000 ELSE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `second or subsequent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `suing or enforcing during the moratorium` THEN 0
    WHEN `calling a performance bond early` THEN 0
    WHEN `forfeiting or not restoring an event deposit` THEN 0
    WHEN `a false declaration for rental relief` THEN 12
    WHEN `a false declaration for rental waiver` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE IF `second or subsequent` THEN 12 ELSE 6
